{
  "id": 272733041,
  "iid": 13835,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Don't pass UTF_8 arg to valgrind script",
  "description": "The `CHECK_UTF_8` arg is a long-style `--` arg which the valgrind script doesn't know how to deal with, so just skip it while fuzzing under valgrind. Basically this means that `-g` implies `-U` in the fuzz script. Otherwise you get failures like\n```\n$ ../tools/fuzz-test.sh -g ~/Downloads/0012_-_usb_hci_win_test_2.pcapng \nASan enabled. Virtual memory limit is unlimited\nRunning ../tools/valgrind-wireshark.sh -b run --log-fatal-domains=UTF-8  with args: \"\"\n\"-T\"\n(forever)\n\nPass 1:\n    0012_-_usb_hci_win_test_2.pcapng: () (-T) ../tools/fuzz-test.sh: line 307: [: -ne: unary operator expected\n../tools/fuzz-test.sh: line 307: [: -ne: unary operator expected\n OK (0 seconds)\n```\n\n(The actual error from the valgrind script is hidden, but is the more understandable `Unknown option: -`)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-12-31T14:26:40.053Z",
